chive_unavailable","receiptSha256":"4d3654aabbd278b441113fd2849c2921b159283130e3ff174337511c4b78ce11"}],"limitation":"No verified image is imported. Existing neutral placeholder; not proof that no cover exists at the provider or elsewhere."}],"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-11-03T09:26:38.922Z","review_batch":"nl-scale-20261102-047"}},{"ref":"d6","relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","key":{"work_id":987146012,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":987146012,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":987346007,"text":"Christopher Browning onderzoekt hoe de mannen van Reservepolitiebataljon 101 betrokken raakten bij de massamoord op Joden in bezet Polen. Hij volgt hun optreden bij executies en deportaties in 1942 en analyseert de keuzes die zij maakten. Daarbij kijkt hij onder meer naar groepsdruk, gehoorzaamheid aan gezag en veranderende morele normen. Het boek vraagt hoe mensen die niet allemaal als fanatieke nazi''s begonnen toch aan vernietiging deelnamen. Browning verbindt concrete historische gebeurtenissen met een onderzoek naar verantwoordelijkheid en aanpassing.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Gecontroleerde boek- en catalogusbronnen","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL85351W","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p427681472"],"checked_at":"2026-11-03T09:26:38.922Z","reference":"work:3260","note":"Retain existing Work3260 Ordinary Men / Christopher R. Browning and exact Dutch Doodgewone mannen 9789401917223 Paperback. KB original-title/volume and existing source-edition parent compared; original content review content-review-023.json retained. No abridgment, omnibus or translated-title duplication established for this selected edition. This changes presentation metadata/summary only; do not claim additionalDutchavailability.","canonical_name_resolution":null},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","review":"content-review-023.json","sources":